{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>After this manner did your servant to me.</b> This is a proof for what the Sages, of blessed memory, expounded, that he was a saris (eunuch) and was unable to perform intercourse, and from here they expounded, of blessed memory: 'at the time of intimacy she said to him.' And the intention is not actual intercourse, since he was a saris, but the intimacy was in types of fondling — in embracing and kissing. For if it had been actual intercourse, how is it possible that she would confess to what never was and thereby be held in contempt in her husband's eyes? And if the matter were true, it would have been fitting for her to conceal it — how would she lie to fabricate against him and thereby blemish herself? Rather, the meaning of <b>after this manner</b> is in types of fondling: for this wicked woman fabricated against Joseph that he came upon her and forced himself upon her in types of fondling and embraces like his own."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:18:55.275851666Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}